#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""One-off conversion from the checkout install to the operator app.

This script is not part of the permanent bootstrap, the `agents/matuto/` package
or any release file; it is deleted after the operator's cutover, beside
`cutover/matuto-cutover`. It reads the old layout as data and changes none of it:

* `profiles/`, `speech-profiles/`, `bundles/` and `defaults.sh` are parsed as
  plain text. Nothing is sourced, evaluated or executed, and a file holding
  anything but a plain variable or array assignment is refused naming the file
  and line while every other file still converts.
* One import document in the store's format is emitted from the profiles, the
  bundles and the card and speech executables the operator names, so a new
  language profile or bundle arrives as an unpublished candidate. No
  qualification state, alias publication or build provenance is carried.
* Every old value that is not carried is listed by file and name in the report
  with the reason it was not, and nothing is invented for a value the old file
  does not state.
* The old results directories and the privately archived run records are
  imported once as legacy runs through the store module, in one transaction each
  and with no fingerprint: browsable and downloadable, never citable.

The document is imported before the legacy runs, because the store refuses a new
record whose stable ID retained run evidence already holds.
"""

